    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 89,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Publish 1.x built by core** (`make core_publish`): the steps and their owners are on the \"Publish 1.x from core\" card in WEB-startr.style.core/TODO.md"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 90,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "1.4.0 live 2026-10-16 (tag v1.4.0): /style.css b845cff\u2026, /startr.css and /props.json from core; /style-core/ pages styled again"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 91,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Move the /style.min.css consumers to the 1.4.0 min after a visual check** (Sage.is, Startr.cloud): the rolling min still serves the drifted 1.3.2 bytes; 1.4.0's min changes about 250 element rules for them (body, h4, pre, forms, tables)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 93,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "[MANUALLY] **Narrow the Cloudflare image rule**: a redirect rule on the startr.style zone (not Netlify: no x-nf-request-id) sends dotted first segments to image.startr.cloud, and real files do not shadow it; /v1.3.2/ and /v1.4.0/ 302 (2026-10-16). Match numeric WxH only"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 94,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Ship pinned and rolling CDN versions**: Currently unversioned \u2014 any change to Startr.Style hits every consumer (Sage.is, Sage.Education) instantly, with no rollback path. Publish `/v1/`, `/v2/`, and a rolling `/latest/`. Implementation approach: submodule structure where `v1/` is a submodule pointing to the project at the v1 tag, `v2/` at v2, etc. \u2014 versioned URLs serve from the pinned submodule, `latest/` serves from `master`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 95,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Consumers pin to a version in prod; `latest` is for the Startr studio itself. Migration plan needed for existing Sage.is / Sage.Education `<link>` tags currently pointing at the unversioned URL. *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman in a panel review of Sage.is, 2026-04-18.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 96,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Cache headers \u2014 versioned vs rolling**: `/v1/style.css`, `/v2/style.css`, etc. \u2192 `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` (one year, immutable; the URL's contents never change by design). `/latest/style.css` \u2192 `Cache-Control: public, max-age=60, must-revalidate` (short TTL + revalidate so studio pushes propagate quickly and stale copies don't linger). *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman, 2026-04-18.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 97,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Emit SRI integrity hashes for each pinned release**: Generate `sha384` integrity hashes at release time and publish them alongside the versioned URL so consumers can use `<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/v1/style.css\" integrity=\"sha384-...\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">`. Gives consumers an integrity guarantee even though Startr.Style is on a separate origin. *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman, 2026-04-18.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 98,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Resolve version drift between README and package.json**: `README.md` opens with `1.3.1`; `package.json` declares `1.2.2.2`. Pick one source of truth (conventionally `package.json`) and make the README read from it, or bump them in lockstep via `scripts/release.sh`. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "d94da4550632ad9d",
      "line_num": 86,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**\ud83d\udce6 Versioning & Rollback**\n- [x] **Publish 1.x built by core** (`make core_publish`): the steps and their owners are on the \"Publish 1.x from core\" card in WEB-startr.style.core/TODO.md\n- [x] 1.4.0 live 2026-10-16 (tag v1.4.0): /style.css b845cff\u2026, /startr.css and /props.json from core; /style-core/ pages styled again\n- [ ] **Move the /style.min.css consumers to the 1.4.0 min after a visual check** (Sage.is, Startr.cloud): the rolling min still serves the drifted 1.3.2 bytes; 1.4.0's min changes about 250 element rules for them (body, h4, pre, forms, tables)\n- [ ] [MANUALLY] **Narrow the Cloudflare image rule**: a redirect rule on the startr.style zone (not Netlify: no x-nf-request-id) sends dotted first segments to image.startr.cloud, and real files do not shadow it; /v1.3.2/ and /v1.4.0/ 302 (2026-10-16). Match numeric WxH only\n- [ ] **Ship pinned and rolling CDN versions**: Currently unversioned \u2014 any change to Startr.Style hits every consumer (Sage.is, Sage.Education) instantly, with no rollback path. Publish `/v1/`, `/v2/`, and a rolling `/latest/`. Implementation approach: submodule structure where `v1/` is a submodule pointing to the project at the v1 tag, `v2/` at v2, etc. \u2014 versioned URLs serve from the pinned submodule, `latest/` serves from `master`.\n- [ ] Consumers pin to a version in prod; `latest` is for the Startr studio itself. Migration plan needed for existing Sage.is / Sage.Education `<link>` tags currently pointing at the unversioned URL. *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman in a panel review of Sage.is, 2026-04-18.)*\n- [ ] **Cache headers \u2014 versioned vs rolling**: `/v1/style.css`, `/v2/style.css`, etc. \u2192 `Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable` (one year, immutable; the URL's contents never change by design). `/latest/style.css` \u2192 `Cache-Control: public, max-age=60, must-revalidate` (short TTL + revalidate so studio pushes propagate quickly and stale copies don't linger). *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman, 2026-04-18.)*\n- [ ] **Emit SRI integrity hashes for each pinned release**: Generate `sha384` integrity hashes at release time and publish them alongside the versioned URL so consumers can use `<link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"/v1/style.css\" integrity=\"sha384-...\" crossorigin=\"anonymous\">`. Gives consumers an integrity guarantee even though Startr.Style is on a separate origin. *(Surfaced by Zach Leatherman, 2026-04-18.)*\n- [ ] **Resolve version drift between README and package.json**: `README.md` opens with `1.3.1`; `package.json` declares `1.2.2.2`. Pick one source of truth (conventionally `package.json`) and make the README read from it, or bump them in lockstep via `scripts/release.sh`. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*\n\n`TODO.md:L86`",
