    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 102,
          "tags": [
            "#dx",
            "#landmine"
          ],
          "text": "**Give prop typos a failure mode**: An inline prop with no matching `[style*=\"--X:\"]` rule fails silently \u2014 no error, no fallback, the declaration just sits inert. Two real hits in build.sage.education (2026-08-25, commit 3198f0b): `--ovx` written for `--ofx`, `--lst` written for `--lis`; both shipped broken layout and were caught only in a 360px visual pass."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 103,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Publish the canonical prop list as a JSON artifact per release (extractable from the built sheet by regexing `[style*=\"--X:\"]` selectors \u2014 proof-of-concept script exists in build.sage.education's `--br` audit)."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 104,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Core's build writes props.json (every prop, tier, state, collision, deprecation); `make core_publish` copies it to src/static/props.json and src/_data/props.json, and src/docs/utilities.njk renders from it (2026-10-16)"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 105,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "scripts/snapshot-version.sh pins no props.json, so a pinned sheet has no pinned dictionary"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 106,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Authoring-time linter: check every `--*` in template `style=\"\"` attributes against that list; run in consumer CI."
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 107,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Core's `bun run ingest <page>` lints inline props against props.json: unknown, deprecated, collision, tier-state (2026-10-16); consumer CI hookup still open"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 108,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Dev-mode runtime warner: a tiny opt-in script that scans `[style*=\"--\"]` elements and console.warns unknown props."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 109,
          "tags": [
            "#landmine"
          ],
          "text": "**Shorthand dual bindings** (`--br` = border-radius AND border-right; `--bs`, `--td`, `--fs`, `--cr` value-disjoint pairs): the naming decision is filed in `WEB-startr.style.core/TODO.md` \u2014 resolve it there, then mirror the outcome here. Consumers are already routing around the DSL (build.sage.education writes plain `flex-shrink:0` to avoid `--fs`)."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "60b210cd30cb2e5f",
      "line_num": 100,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**\ud83e\udde8 Silent-Failure DX \u2014 unknown props are no-ops**\n- [ ] **Give prop typos a failure mode**: An inline prop with no matching `[style*=\"--X:\"]` rule fails silently \u2014 no error, no fallback, the declaration just sits inert. Two real hits in build.sage.education (2026-08-25, commit 3198f0b): `--ovx` written for `--ofx`, `--lst` written for `--lis`; both shipped broken layout and were caught only in a 360px visual pass. #dx #landmine\n- [x] Publish the canonical prop list as a JSON artifact per release (extractable from the built sheet by regexing `[style*=\"--X:\"]` selectors \u2014 proof-of-concept script exists in build.sage.education's `--br` audit).\n- [x] Core's build writes props.json (every prop, tier, state, collision, deprecation); `make core_publish` copies it to src/static/props.json and src/_data/props.json, and src/docs/utilities.njk renders from it (2026-10-16)\n- [ ] scripts/snapshot-version.sh pins no props.json, so a pinned sheet has no pinned dictionary\n- [ ] Authoring-time linter: check every `--*` in template `style=\"\"` attributes against that list; run in consumer CI.\n- [x] Core's `bun run ingest <page>` lints inline props against props.json: unknown, deprecated, collision, tier-state (2026-10-16); consumer CI hookup still open\n- [ ] Dev-mode runtime warner: a tiny opt-in script that scans `[style*=\"--\"]` elements and console.warns unknown props.\n- [ ] **Shorthand dual bindings** (`--br` = border-radius AND border-right; `--bs`, `--td`, `--fs`, `--cr` value-disjoint pairs): the naming decision is filed in `WEB-startr.style.core/TODO.md` \u2014 resolve it there, then mirror the outcome here. Consumers are already routing around the DSL (build.sage.education writes plain `flex-shrink:0` to avoid `--fs`). #landmine\n\n`TODO.md:L100`",
