    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 113,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Audit `-hvr` coverage for `:focus` and `:focus-visible`**: Every `[style*=\"--X-hvr:\"]:hover` rule should be paired with `:focus, :focus-visible` so keyboard users get the same affordance as mouse users. `--shadow-hvr` covers `:focus` today; audit and enumerate the rest (`--hvr-bgc`, `--hvr-c`, `--hvr-bdc`, etc.). Land coverage systematically, not ad-hoc. *(Surfaced by Adam Wathan in a panel review of Sage.is, 2026-04-18.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 114,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Done in core (2026-10-16): every hover rule, the new `--x-hover` props and the `-hvr`/`-hover` helpers, has a `:focus-visible` copy; scripts/bands.test.ts and states.test.ts hold it"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 115,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Reconcile `:focus-visible` audit status with spoken claims**: The `-hvr` coverage audit above has been open since 2026-04-18, yet a verbal claim of \"keyboard accessibility tested, no issues\" was made during the 2026-04-20 panel. Either close the audit with a landed commit, or retract the claim. Both states cannot be true at once. *(Surfaced by Heydon Pickering in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "6e4764424a11d65a",
      "line_num": 111,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**\u267f Accessibility**\n- [x] **Audit `-hvr` coverage for `:focus` and `:focus-visible`**: Every `[style*=\"--X-hvr:\"]:hover` rule should be paired with `:focus, :focus-visible` so keyboard users get the same affordance as mouse users. `--shadow-hvr` covers `:focus` today; audit and enumerate the rest (`--hvr-bgc`, `--hvr-c`, `--hvr-bdc`, etc.). Land coverage systematically, not ad-hoc. *(Surfaced by Adam Wathan in a panel review of Sage.is, 2026-04-18.)*\n- [x] Done in core (2026-10-16): every hover rule, the new `--x-hover` props and the `-hvr`/`-hover` helpers, has a `:focus-visible` copy; scripts/bands.test.ts and states.test.ts hold it\n- [ ] **Reconcile `:focus-visible` audit status with spoken claims**: The `-hvr` coverage audit above has been open since 2026-04-18, yet a verbal claim of \"keyboard accessibility tested, no issues\" was made during the 2026-04-20 panel. Either close the audit with a landed commit, or retract the claim. Both states cannot be true at once. *(Surfaced by Heydon Pickering in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*\n\n`TODO.md:L111`",
      "type": "text",
      "width": 280,
      "x": 10,
      "y": 240
    },
    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 119,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Audit every colour leaf for IACVT-safe fallbacks**: The 216-cell `color-mix(in oklch, \u2026)` cascade in `src/style-core/src/variables.css` invalidates whole declarations when any component is unparseable. Every consumer leaf (e.g. `background: var(--primary)`) must resolve to `var(--primary, <literal-fallback>)`, not `inherit`/`initial`. Audit the whole leaf surface, not one line \u2014 otherwise the DSL has accents. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 120,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Moot since 2026-10-16: the 216-cell cascade is gone (`--mix`/`--tone` compute on the element); the new tints ship literal defaults with color-mix() under @supports"
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 121,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "**Register critical custom properties with `@property`**: Without registration, the browser treats colour and layout variables as untyped strings. Downstream `color-mix()` and `calc()` can silently IACVT when consumers pass malformed values. Register `--primary`, `--background`, `--text-main`, and the 216-cell cube entries so the browser can validate inputs and animate between them. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*"
        },
        {
          "checked": true,
          "line_num": 122,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`--mix`, `--tone`, `--tone-of`, `--mixed` and `--toned` are registered, inherits:false (2026-10-16); `--primary`, `--background` and `--text-main` are not"
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "607c7cdfe1be3ae1",
      "line_num": 117,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [],
      "text": "**\ud83c\udfa8 Colour System Invariants**\n- [x] **Audit every colour leaf for IACVT-safe fallbacks**: The 216-cell `color-mix(in oklch, \u2026)` cascade in `src/style-core/src/variables.css` invalidates whole declarations when any component is unparseable. Every consumer leaf (e.g. `background: var(--primary)`) must resolve to `var(--primary, <literal-fallback>)`, not `inherit`/`initial`. Audit the whole leaf surface, not one line \u2014 otherwise the DSL has accents. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*\n- [x] Moot since 2026-10-16: the 216-cell cascade is gone (`--mix`/`--tone` compute on the element); the new tints ship literal defaults with color-mix() under @supports\n- [ ] **Register critical custom properties with `@property`**: Without registration, the browser treats colour and layout variables as untyped strings. Downstream `color-mix()` and `calc()` can silently IACVT when consumers pass malformed values. Register `--primary`, `--background`, `--text-main`, and the 216-cell cube entries so the browser can validate inputs and animate between them. *(Surfaced by Lea Verou in a panel review of Startr.Style, 2026-04-20.)*\n- [x] `--mix`, `--tone`, `--tone-of`, `--mixed` and `--toned` are registered, inherits:false (2026-10-16); `--primary`, `--background` and `--text-main` are not\n\n`TODO.md:L117`",
