    {
      "children": [
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 78,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "`swap:after` and `adoptScripts` run after `transition(run)` returns, but `startViewTransition` runs the callback asynchronously: under a View Transition the event precedes the DOM update and `pushState`. Move both inside the callback."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 79,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Decide whether the library re-creates inline `<script>` elements in a swapped region; the host workaround is `src/_includes/swap-host.njk`."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 80,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Add a `License: MIT` line to the `/*!` header. It changes the pin, so every consumer re-pins once."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 81,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Make the comments ASCII-only: 173 `\u2500` rulers, 18 em dashes and one `\u2026` (192 non-ASCII characters, none in code). A host that serves `.js` without a charset shows them as `\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6` in the raw view; Netlify sends `charset=UTF-8`, the Eleventy dev server does not. Saves about 500 bytes raw. Same pin change as the header line, so ship both together."
        },
        {
          "checked": false,
          "line_num": 82,
          "tags": [],
          "text": "Have AI-UI's `scripts/gates/startr-swap/check.py` compare its copy against `https://startr.style/v1/swap.js.sha256` so the two cannot drift silently."
        }
      ],
      "file_path": "TODO.md",
      "height": 80,
      "id": "cc89e5db69b41f34",
      "line_num": 77,
      "source": "todo_md",
      "tags": [
        "#library"
      ],
      "text": "**\ud83d\udd27 v1.1 \u2014 first changes at the new source of truth.**\n- [ ] `swap:after` and `adoptScripts` run after `transition(run)` returns, but `startViewTransition` runs the callback asynchronously: under a View Transition the event precedes the DOM update and `pushState`. Move both inside the callback.\n- [ ] Decide whether the library re-creates inline `<script>` elements in a swapped region; the host workaround is `src/_includes/swap-host.njk`.\n- [ ] Add a `License: MIT` line to the `/*!` header. It changes the pin, so every consumer re-pins once.\n- [ ] Make the comments ASCII-only: 173 `\u2500` rulers, 18 em dashes and one `\u2026` (192 non-ASCII characters, none in code). A host that serves `.js` without a charset shows them as `\u00e2\u20ac\u00a6` in the raw view; Netlify sends `charset=UTF-8`, the Eleventy dev server does not. Saves about 500 bytes raw. Same pin change as the header line, so ship both together.\n- [ ] Have AI-UI's `scripts/gates/startr-swap/check.py` compare its copy against `https://startr.style/v1/swap.js.sha256` so the two cannot drift silently.\n\n`#library`\n`TODO.md:L77`",
